        "c27833cf-7032-4593-870c-f80706b24058": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 32,
            "width": 832,
            "height": 288,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe flow provokes its own post: the **bot** publishes it, the **user account** reads it.\n\n- Public channel `@appmixerE2Evladimir` must exist and `@appmixer_test_bot` must be one of its administrators with the *Post messages* and *Delete messages* rights. On another tenant, create a public channel, add your bot as an administrator and replace the username in SendMessage, NewChannelPost, the Assert and DeleteMessage.\n- Two accounts: a **Telegram** bot account (SendMessage, DeleteMessage) and a **Telegram User** account (NewChannelPost).\n- **Do not remove the Wait.** Flow start records the newest post as the trigger's baseline; a post published before that is never emitted.\n- The cleanup deletes the post by the ID the trigger emitted, so it also proves the trigger fired."
        }
    }
